# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: vl-infp-vl-nanp-exist-on-autocad -- the spec lists them BricsCAD-only; AutoCAD 2022 has both
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: spec
#+DATE: 2026-10-04

* Symptom

probes/sources/probe-versions.lsp on AutoCAD 2022 (job 16921684058):
(type vl-infp) and (type vl-nanp) are SUBR. The spec's Availability lists
both as BricsCAD-only (BricsCAD release notes: added in V21.1.04), so
autolisp-runtime/source/operator-availability.lisp (generated from the
spec) gives them owner :bricscad and the `[vendor-operator]' notice fires
under the AutoCAD dialects for operators AutoCAD has.

* Fix

Correct the two Function Entries' Availability in the autolisp-spec (both
vendors; AutoCAD version of introduction not documented -- measured present
on 2022), regenerate (make -C clautolisp operator-availability), check that
nothing else in the same family is mislabelled: the same probe shows
VLA-POSTCOMMAND, DUMPALLPROPERTIES and GETPROPERTYVALUE present on AutoCAD
2022 too (the last two as EXRXSUBR) -- verify their Availability rows.
